A||N||2||GT-maniac||Fuel pump problems ||||1||
Z||000000||GT-maniac||08-06-2001||10:45 PM||||I can't get my car to start and I think it's a fuel problem. When I turn the ignition on I'm supposed to hear the fuel pump run for about 2 seconds right ? I don't hear anything. I shorted the fuel pump relay like it says to do in the haynes manual and I can hear a clicking sound from behind the battery but it doesn't sound like the pumps going. And the car still won't fire even with the relay shorted to run the pump all the time. Also anybody know where this fuel pump test terminal is that they show in the book ? I don't see it on my 87 GT. I've got good spark so my ignition seems to be okay. I was having problems with the car running for awhile and then just dying unexpectedly.<BR>Seems like a non functioning fuel pump is the likely culprit, does anyone else have any more tests to make sure ?.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steve Normington||08-07-2001||12:13 AM||||The fuel pump test terminal is the one that you are shorting to in the ALDL connector. If you read 12 V on this line, then the pump is getting power. If you short 12 V to this line, then you are running the pump manually. If you are not hearing the fuel pump run when you short the fuel pump test line, then it is most likely the pump or wiring. I don't know of a good way to test it any further w/o dropping the tank.||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||08-07-2001||12:25 AM||||I'm wondering what the clicking sound is behind the battery. fp relay is on the opposite side. Only thing near battery remotly related to the fp is the oil press sw. But all in all, I echo fuel pump /wiring as above.  Is it just me or do similar problems seem to be contagious? One person has a cooling problem, 3 days go by and there are 2-3 more people posting same or similar. Right now fuel pump/ fuel pump fuse blowing 'illness's seems epidemic.<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 08-07-2001).]||||reg||1
